cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "POP de Elite: drafting institutional quality documents from a conversation"
message: >-
  If this software is useful in your work, a citation is appreciated.
  It is asked for, not required by the licence.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Braga"
    given-names: "Henrique Faria"
    website: "https://radioterapia.ai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/radioterapia-ai/Pop-de-Elite"
url: "https://radioterapia.ai"
abstract: >-
  A web tool that drafts institutional quality documents for hospitals and
  clinics: standard operating procedures, policies, protocols, checklists,
  consent form templates and other supporting documents, with a management
  sheet and a training deck where they apply. A conversation collects the
  process, the roles and the risks; a document engine builds Word, Excel and
  PowerPoint files, including BPMN-style flowcharts with swimlanes. The
  language model is Google Gemini, a third-party service. Every output is a
  draft for the institution's own review. Not a medical device, and not
  validated for clinical use.
keywords:
  - quality management
  - patient safety
  - standard operating procedure
  - hospital
  - document generation
  - radiation therapy
license: Apache-2.0
